                <pb facs="0194" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/483: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-14T09:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                                1927—9 a.m.</hi></date> [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >sic</hi>]<lb/>[Received 9:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>218. My 214, March 14, 5 p.m. Following from Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 13, noon. Ch’en sent telegraphic instructions last night to
                            Commissioner Foreign Affairs and Political Bureau at Foochow directing
                            that special efforts be made to adequately protect life and property
                            Americans in that region. Price informed.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
